# Mambo A Go-Go (GQA40 VER. JRB, Rental), Konami 2001: the next boot, from what mamboagga-install left (its NVRAM).
# The flash checksums, ERROR 198 again (no e-Amusement device): Start at 1000; NOTE 605 (RTC-RAM
# cleared): Test at 1500; BOOT CHECK, then "HARD-WARE ERROR +02H, RTCRAM INITIALIZE ERROR, PLEASE
# CALL ATTENDANT" by frame ~3900, where it stays (the JAB version passes its BOOT CHECK here). Hashes
# the main RAM every frame and snapshots every 60 frames, to compare HIRAKU's 573 core with MAME.
game mamboagga

hash ram  0x80000000 0x80400000   # 4 MiB main RAM (KSEG0)

at 1000 press "1 Player Start" 8   # ERROR 198
at 1500 press "Service Mode" 8     # NOTE 605
from 0 every 60 snap
at 4800 quit
